  "content": {
    "id": "p37-q15",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Use the fact that $|-x|=|x|$ to decide whether these functions are odd, even or neither.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 4,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p37-q15-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=|x|+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Even.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=|-x|+1\\\\f(-x)&=|x|+1\\\\f(-x)&=f(x)\\end{align*}$$Therefore $f$ is even.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "p37-q15-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=|x|+x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Neither.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=|-x|-x\\\\f(-x)&=|x|-x\\end{align*}$$For example, $f(1)=2$ and $f(-1)=0$. These values satisfy neither $f(-1)=f(1)$ nor $f(-1)=-f(1)$, so $f$ is neither even nor odd.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 19
      },
      {
        "id": "p37-q15-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=x\\times|x|$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Odd.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=(-x)|-x|\\\\f(-x)&=-x|x|\\\\f(-x)&=-f(x)\\end{align*}$$Therefore $f$ is odd.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "p37-q15-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=|x^3-x|$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Even.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=|(-x)^3-(-x)|\\\\f(-x)&=|-x^3+x|\\\\f(-x)&=|-(x^3-x)|\\\\f(-x)&=|x^3-x|\\\\f(-x)&=f(x)\\end{align*}$$Therefore $f$ is even.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 17
      }
    ]
  },
